{% extends "_base.txt.j2" %}
{% set kicker = "ATTESTATION REVOKED" %}
{% set headline = "ZKP attestation has been revoked" %}
{% block body %}
A zero-knowledge proof attestation issued by an agent under your developer
account has been revoked. Verifications now fail with verified=false,
revoked=true; downstream consumers (auditors, dispute referees, governance
modules) will see the revocation immediately.

  Attestation ID:  {{ attestation_id }}
  Agent DID:       {{ agent_did }}
  Revoked at:      {{ revoked_at }}
  Revoked by:      {{ revoked_by }}
  Reason:          {{ revoked_reason }}

Open record: {{ registry_ui_url }}#/attestations/{{ attestation_id }}

If this revocation was unintended, contact your registry admin. Revocation
is final on the protocol layer; a fresh proof must be generated and
re-submitted to restore standing.
{% endblock %}
